WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:07.500
Hi, I'm Chase. I'm going to go over my
A-Dartment auto-scoring dartboard.

2
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:16.200
It's mostly inspired by Autodarts,
and a lot of it was coded using Claude.

3
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.000
We got the Spartan to hold the darts,
that was found online.

4
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.700
And then I hand-drew the little
dashboard and scoreboard.

5
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.800
I need to import the records.
Let's go reset that.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.800
Over here with the dartboard,
I 3D printed the different mounts.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.500
They all hold a 32 by 32 camera
from Amazon.

8
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.900
Each one of the mounts
is a different iteration.

9
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.600
This one is the best. It has the lip
that hooks onto the ring around the edge.

10
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.100
Then it all wires down
to a Raspberry Pi down there.

11
00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:02.400
The accuracy for scoring is 90-something.

12
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:16.900
Originally, I just had the detection of the darts,
and it just takes the different camera angles.

13
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:26.700
Eventually, I needed to implement a model to detect
the very tip of the dart and where it landed,

14
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:35.000
because when it got to the triples and on the edges,
it was hit or miss.

15
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.300
We'll go ahead and throw a couple.

16
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.000
That's 10.

17
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.500
16, 1.

18
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.700
So we got 15, 16, 1.

19
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.000
There's the 90% accuracy for you.

20
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.700
And then it switches over to Cade's turn.

21
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.000
Grab a couple darts.

22
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.300
Triple 20s, maybe? Just 20.

23
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.500
Five.

24
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.900
So that was 25 and 25.

25
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.500
Let's see what we got here. Hey, look at that.

26
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.300
25 and 25.

27
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:40.800
That is the A-Dartment auto-scoring project for you.
